<sn><md>#### List a Local Folder

You can also use `rclone ls` with local paths:

```bash
emon@emon:~$ ls
Desktop  Documents  Downloads  Field  Music  Pictures  Public  Templates  Videos  snap
emon@emon:~$ rclone ls Documents
      567 bcs learning setup for linux.md
       18 note.txt
       27 note2.md
       36 syllabus.md
        0 Books/Chemistry.pdf
        0 Books/Math.pdf
        0 Books/Physics.pdf
        0 Books/Notes/chemistry_note.md
        0 Books/Notes/math_note.md
        0 Books/Notes/physics_note.md
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### List a Remote Folder

This lists **all files** in your Google Drive remote.

```text
emon@emon:~$ rclone ls gd:Notes
        0 math_note.md
        0 physics_note.md
        0 chemistry_note.md
       -1 FolderA/Untitled document.docx
       -1 FolderA/FolderB/Untitled presentation.pptx
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### List Files in a Specific Folder

For example:

```bash
emon@emon:~$ rclone ls gd:Notes/FolderA
       -1 Untitled document.docx
       -1 FolderB/Untitled presentation.pptx
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### List Files Recursively

`rclone ls` searches **recursively by default**. For example:

```bash
rclone ls gdrive:Documents
```

can display:

```text
Documents/
├── notes.txt
├── image.jpg
└── Study/
    ├── chapter1.pdf
    └── chapter2.pdf
```

The actual output will show paths rather than a graphical tree:

```text
     2048 notes.txt
   1048576 image.jpg
    524288 Study/chapter1.pdf
    734003 Study/chapter2.pdf
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Useful Related Commands

| Command       | Lists                     | Recursive    |
| ------------- | ------------------------- | ------------ |
| `rclone ls`   | Files with sizes          | ✅ Yes        |
| `rclone lsd`  | Directories               | ❌ No         |
| `rclone lsf`  | Files and directories     | Configurable |
| `rclone size` | Total file count and size | N/A          |
| `rclone tree` | Directory tree            | Configurable |
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Important

The trailing colon matters:

```text
gdrive:
```

means the root of your configured remote.

Without the colon:

```text
gdrive
```

Rclone may interpret it as a **local path** instead of your configured remote.
</md></sn>